From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat: three answers to the only question the client
 opens the portal for
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Attention, calm and degraded are different content, not styling variants,
and the component only dispatches — the rule that separates them lives in
the domain, because the phase 16 email and any later assistant read the
same decision and a second implementation is where divergence starts.

The attention slab keeps its language: navy, eyes looking down at the
number, the padded numeral, a full-width call to action on mobile. What
changed is where the items come from. The first item dominates and the rest
collapse into compact rows, because a column of giant numbers answers
nothing.

Calm is not an empty state, and that distinction is the reason it exists.
It is the answer to "is anything waiting for me?", so it never disappears —
if it did, the client would go hunting through the system, which is the
behaviour this phase exists to end. It is also the most seen block in the
product, since most visits happen when nothing is pending, so it gets the
same care as the slab in an inverted register. A paused project does not
say everything is fine; it says it is paused, and it does not repeat the
current stage, which would assert work that stopped.

Degraded says the reading failed without saying anything technical, and
without alarm: no alert role, no error colour, no retry button for a
failure the client did not cause. A component test asserts the calm phrases
appear nowhere in its tree.

